course: dictionary
lesson: 11399
title: Accompaniment: what goes with what
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An accompaniment is something that goes along with something else, usually to support it. «The singer had a piano accompaniment.» The piano plays behind the singer and supports the song, so an accompaniment is the music that goes with the main tune. Look for the clue: the singer is the main part, and the piano goes along with it.
explain: Food can have an accompaniment too. «Chips are a good accompaniment to fish.» The chips do not replace the fish. They go with it, like a side dish. Ask yourself: is one thing the main part, with another thing going along with it? If yes, the other thing is an accompaniment.
explain: The phrase «to the accompaniment of» means while a sound is going on. «The children sang to the accompaniment of rain on the roof.» The rain was falling at the same time as the singing. Check by swapping in «while»: «The children sang while rain fell on the roof» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Accompaniment is a noun: an accompaniment, accompaniments.
fact: «Accompaniment» means music played to support a singer or another instrument.
fact: «Accompaniment» can also mean something that goes well with something else, especially food.
fact: «To the accompaniment of» means while a sound is going on, as in «to the accompaniment of cheers».
fact: «Without accompaniment» means sung or played alone, with no music behind it.
exercise: «The choir sang beautifully with piano accompaniment.» What is the accompaniment here? | *The piano music that supports the singing | The audience's clapping | The sheet music | The choir
exercise: «Rice is a tasty accompaniment to curry.» What does accompaniment mean here? | A rival dish | *Something served with the curry to go with it | Something that makes the curry cold | A kind of spice
exercise: «The show began to the accompaniment of loud drums.» What does this phrase mean? | *While the drums were playing | Before the drums broke | Instead of the drums | Without any sound at all
test: «She sang her song without accompaniment.» What does this tell you about the song? | It had a full band | It was played very quietly on a drum | It was sung backwards | *It was sung alone, with no music behind it
test: Mia says, «The soup came with warm bread, a lovely accompaniment.» What is the bread? | A kind of plate | *Something that goes with the soup | A sort of spoon | The main dish
exam: Ana writes, «The waves crashed to the accompaniment of seagulls.» Which word could replace «to the accompaniment of» without changing the meaning? | Instead of | Without | Before | *While
